+Feature: Manage Todos
+  As a user
+  I want to create, edit, and delete todo items
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: New todo creation
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo by pressing Enter
+    Given the todo input is focused
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the todo input and press Enter
+    Then "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+    And the todo input is cleared
+    And #main and #footer are visible
+
+  Scenario: Do not create empty todos
+    Given the todo input is focused
+    When I type "   " into the todo input and press Enter
+    Then no new todo is added to the list
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace from new todo title
+    Given the todo input is focused
+    When I type "  Walk the dog  " into the todo input and press Enter
+    Then "Walk the dog" appears in the todo list
+
+  Rule: Hidden containers
+
+  Scenario: Hide main and footer when no todos exist
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    Then #main is hidden
+    And #footer is hidden
+
+  Rule: Todo item interactions
+
+  Scenario: Delete a todo by clicking the destroy button
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    When I click the destroy button on "Buy groceries"
+    Then "Buy groceries" is removed from the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Double-click a todo label to enter editing mode
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo item has the editing class
+    And the edit input is focused
+    And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+
+  Rule: Edit a todo
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy food" and press Enter
+    Then "Buy food" appears in the todo list
+    And "Buy groceries" is not in the todo list
+    And the editing class is removed
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy food" and blur the input
+    Then "Buy food" appears in the todo list
+    And the editing class is removed
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo when edit is emptied
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I clear the edit input and press Enter
+    Then "Buy groceries" is removed from the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace from edited title
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "  Buy food  " and press Enter
+    Then "Buy food" appears in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Discard edit on Escape
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy food" and press Escape
+    Then "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+    And the editing class is removed
+
+  Rule: Counter
+
+  Scenario: Show remaining count
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+    And "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When I view the todo count
+    Then the count shows "1"
+    And the count label says "item"
+
+  Scenario: Pluralize item count
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+    When I view the todo count
+    Then the count shows "2"
+    And the count label says "items"
+
+  Scenario: Show zero items left
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When I view the todo count
+    Then the count shows "0"
+    And the count label says "items"
\ No newline at end of file
