+Feature: Filter Todos by Route
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by route
+  So that I can see all, active, or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo list contains "Pay bills"
+    And "Pay bills" is completed
+
+  Rule: Default route shows all
+
+  Scenario: Show all todos by default
+    Given the route is "#/"
+    Then all 3 todos are visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: All filter link is selected by default
+    Given the route is "#/"
+    Then the "All" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Filter active todos
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then only active todos are visible
+    And completed todos are hidden
+    And the "Active" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Filter completed todos
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then only completed todos are visible
+    And active todos are hidden
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Persist filter on reload
+
+  Scenario: Persist active filter across reloads
+    Given I navigate to "#/active"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the route is "#/active"
+    And only active todos are visible
+
+  Rule: Item update in filtered state
+
+  Scenario: Completed item hidden when in active filter
+    Given I navigate to "#/active"
+    When I click the checkbox on "Walk the dog"
+    Then "Walk the dog" is hidden from the list
+
+  Scenario: Active item hidden when in completed filter
+    Given I navigate to "#/completed"
+    When I click the checkbox on "Pay bills"
+    Then "Pay bills" is hidden from the list
\ No newline at end of file
